// CotSC: English translation extracted from beregost_v75_npcs.d
// Original English strings preserved exactly. Translate text inside ~...~ only.

@1 = ~The sirines inside the Song of the Morning Temple are so beautiful. You could get lost in their otherworldly voices. But I can't help wondering: how can they survive so far from water? And why do they obey a mere human?~
@2 = ~I guess even Lathander's priests have a dark side. My bet is he imprisoned 'em and keeps 'em enthralled for his own twisted pleasures. Mayhap ye don't know yer own priest all that well.~
@3 = ~A highly improbable theory, halfling. Kelddath possesses considerable divine power, which he may well use to sustain them far from a natural body of water. Such a feat is entirely possible for a cleric of his abilities. Why am I not surprised that your warped mind leapt to such a base conclusion?~
@4 = ~Shut it, ye harpy! At least I ain't keepin' some stutterin' would-be knight in shinin' armour around just 'cause I'm afraid o' a little loneliness.~
@5 = ~T-that was absolutely u-u-uncalled for!~
@6 = ~Ahem, Kagain... it's so nice to see you! How have you been?~
@7 = ~Oh, Kagain is such a... sweet man. So handsome, too...~
@8 = ~Nooo! I... me? I would never do that. I only want to make sure you're... safe.~
@9 = ~Pretty well, Kava. I hope you haven't been... looking through my window to watch me work lately.~
@10 = ~My safety is compromised because of that crazy stalker.~
@11 = ~Oooh, isn't that sweet? You have a fanbase.~
@12 = ~Quite the opposite. It's horrid. The only love I seek is the love of money. I don't care for any of that trivial love life so many people desperately pursue nowadays. And I'd like to keep it that way.~
@13 = ~I've just made a wine from yeast and honey. Would you like to taste it? It's my great-grandmother's recipe. She was a professional winemaker in Berdusk. You'll love it, I guarantee it!~
@14 = ~Erm... yeah, sure.~
@15 = ~I don't drink. Alcohol makes me nauseated.~
@16 = ~I think I'll have to refuse.~
@17 = ~Here you go! I should warn you, though: it's got quite a kick.~
@18 = ~Oh, I understand. More for the rest of us, then!~
@19 = ~As you wish. Perhaps another time.~
@20 = ~Leave some fer me, necromancer! She didn't give it just fer ye!~
@21 = ~Silence, Monty! Real men are drowning their sorrows in a bottle here!~
@22 = ~Ye'll feel real sorrow soon enough, wizard—when ye're pushin' up daisies! Hand it over!~
@23 = ~It's sour. And so... bitter. Ew! How do people drink this stuff?~
@24 = ~(He smiles.) Heh, Imoen, this is what adults d-drink to relieve tension and bury their worries. W-wines have distinct tastes, after all.~
@25 = ~I know what wine tastes like, silly! I've had some before, when Puffguts wasn't looking. But this... tastes wrong. Try it yourself, you'll see!~
@26 = ~(He takes a sip and nearly spits it out.) By the g-gods! What is this? It tastes like... old socks mixed with kobold faeces!~
@27 = ~Oh, enough, both of you! You are behaving like children. Your palates simply aren't accustomed to an unfamiliar flavour. (She takes a sip, and her expression twists into a stunned grimace.) Oh... well. I suppose I stand corrected. Perhaps we should drink no more of this.~
@28 = ~Agreed!~
@29 = ~My mum worries about my father. He had to go away on business for a while. But he can defend himself, so I'm not worried! He told me stories about his adventures. He fought a cyclops, a giant—even a dragon!~
@30 = ~I am certain he did all of that. Not a shadow of doubt in my mind.~
@31 = ~Don't worry, child. I'm sure your father is doing well.~
@32 = ~A child's imagination can run wild. Let us hope his father makes it home in one piece.~
